WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.043
I am Sir Jeffrey, a knight of the royal court of England in the twelfth century.

2
00:00:06.044 --> 00:00:12.519
The twelfth century was the High Middle Ages when noble men in shining armor ruled the land.

3
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.570
My story is full of the adventures and glory that only a knight could have known.

4
00:00:17.571 --> 00:00:23.582
I spent years on the Second and Third Crusades, fighting to capture the city of Jerusalem.

5
00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:27.920
This city had been occupied for many years by Arab Muslims.

6
00:00:27.921 --> 00:00:37.656
So, in 1187, Pope Gregory VIII stated that all knights should ride across Europe to the Middle East and take the city.

7
00:00:37.657 --> 00:00:42.726
But before I could do that, I had to spend many years becoming a knight.

8
00:00:42.727 --> 00:00:47.027
I began my journey to knighthood as a page at the age of seven.

9
00:00:47.028 --> 00:00:49.956
I left home to live at the castle of a lord.

10
00:00:49.957 --> 00:00:59.957
As a page, I played many training games with other pages, such as wrestling, sword fighting, and lance practice.

11
00:00:59.958 --> 00:01:04.970
When we practiced sword and lance skills, we used wooden weapons to be safe.

12
00:01:04.971 --> 00:01:09.327
My other lessons involved the lady and lord of the castle.

13
00:01:09.328 --> 00:01:13.528
I would spend the day serving my lord in all things.

14
00:01:13.529 --> 00:01:18.366
If his armor was rusted or dirty, it was my job to clean it.

15
00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:24.569
My lord taught me how to hunt, usually with a bow and arrow, but also with a hawk.

16
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:30.163
The lady of the castle showed me how to be a gentleman by teaching me good manners.

17
00:01:30.164 --> 00:01:37.793
This was very important because a knight is not only a warrior, but a noble person who always does what is right.

18
00:01:37.794 --> 00:01:42.540
Another big part of my day involved learning about God and religion.

19
00:01:42.541 --> 00:01:49.294
This was important because many knights, including myself, were deeply religious Christians.

20
00:01:49.295 --> 00:01:55.225
When I was 14, I was chosen to become a squire, a knight's servant or apprentice.

21
00:01:55.226 --> 00:01:59.787
A squire takes care of the knight's weapons and carries them for him.

22
00:01:59.788 --> 00:02:07.386
In battle, the squire quickly replaces any damaged shield or armor, so the knight can continue fighting.

23
00:02:07.387 --> 00:02:13.420
During my time as a squire, I learned the ways of combat and warfare from my lord.

24
00:02:13.421 --> 00:02:19.363
Now, instead of training with wooden weapons, the other squires and I used real ones.

25
00:02:19.364 --> 00:02:27.354
We studied siege warfare, or how to surround and blockade a city, and the art of commanding soldiers.

26
00:02:27.355 --> 00:02:33.930
As squires, we became expert horsemen. We learned to ride horses and fight at the same time.

27
00:02:33.931 --> 00:02:37.313
We also practiced fighting while wearing heavy armor.

28
00:02:37.314 --> 00:02:43.687
Sometimes during a battle, we were allowed to fight alongside our lord instead of just serving him.

29
00:02:43.688 --> 00:02:47.996
A squire could become a knight between the ages of eighteen and twenty.

30
00:02:47.997 --> 00:02:55.266
When I was thought worthy of becoming a knight, I did everything a squire must do just before a knighting ceremony.

31
00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:59.366
I prayed throughout the night, refusing to eat or sleep.

32
00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:04.872
When morning came, I took a warm bath and put on a special padded vest and hood.

33
00:03:04.873 --> 00:03:09.883
Next, I put on my full armor, which was well-polished and shiny.

34
00:03:09.884 --> 00:03:14.034
Over this armor, I put on a fine white tunic or shirt.

35
00:03:14.035 --> 00:03:20.658
White was the color of purity. I was finally ready to be knighted, or "dubbed," a knight.

36
00:03:20.659 --> 00:03:28.126
For the ceremony, I knelt before my lord and I received my sword, my lance, and golden spurs.

37
00:03:28.127 --> 00:03:34.651
I recited a special oath, or promise, to be loyal and obey him in all things.

38
00:03:34.652 --> 00:03:46.142
I also took the oath of chivalry to protect the weak and defenseless, defend the church, speak the truth, respect women, and live an honorable life.

39
00:03:46.143 --> 00:03:54.934
Then the lord performing the ceremony touched me on the shoulders with a sword and said, "I dub thee Sir Knight."

40
00:03:54.935 --> 00:04:00.127
I had knelt as a squire, but I rose as a knight.

41
00:04:00.128 --> 00:04:07.588
As a knight, I was free to travel, but I always had to be available for my lord in both peace and in war.

42
00:04:07.589 --> 00:04:12.600
But most of the time, before I went on the Crusades, I fought in tournaments.

43
00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:19.209
Tournaments were very common events that allowed knights to compete against each other in combat with swords and lances.

44
00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:24.762
Even though the competitions were games, they were very dangerous and many knights died.

45
00:04:24.763 --> 00:04:30.121
These events could determine a knight's fortune, since knights often bet their wealth on a tournament.

46
00:04:30.122 --> 00:04:33.515
To be beaten was to lose money and reputation.

47
00:04:33.516 --> 00:04:37.480
To win was to gain wealth and fame.

48
00:04:37.481 --> 00:04:40.889
After the Crusades, I eventually returned to England.

49
00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:46.476
I continued to participate in tournaments and fight wars to gain land and money.

50
00:04:46.477 --> 00:04:51.318
I even taught my own pages and squires as I had been taught.

51
00:04:51.319 --> 00:05:03.490
When I look back on my life, I am proud to say that I was a true knight, performed my duties well, and fought for my beliefs.

